WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.333
One block finds the largest score in the

00:00:03.333 --> 00:00:05.812
row. Here, that maximum is one thousand.

00:00:10.312 --> 00:00:12.872
Subtracting the maximum gives zero for

00:00:12.872 --> 00:00:15.859
columns zero and two. Which columns will

00:00:15.859 --> 00:00:17.139
have equal probabilities?

00:00:25.639 --> 00:00:28.499
The two zero shifts have the same

00:00:28.499 --> 00:00:30.950
exponential, one. Dividing by the shared

00:00:30.950 --> 00:00:33.401
row sum gives those columns equal

00:00:33.401 --> 00:00:33.810
probabilities.
